WEBVTT

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:23.540
Announcing the arrival of Japan Air Splendor
flight 1123 arriving from Seattle...

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.910
Too loud! Aya!

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.250
Oh, welcome home!

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.670
Yeah, I'm back!

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.080
Dad!

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:42.340
Aya-chan's father came back to Japan
for the first time in two years!

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.140
Dad, how was Patagonia?

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:49.730
There were tons of animals that weren't in Africa.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:51.620
Take a look!

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.730
Wow! So many alpacas!

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.500
That's not an alpaca. That's a guanaco.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.070
Huh...?

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.990
Aya-chan's father is
a famous animal photographer.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.830
He travels all over the world.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.410
Ah!

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:10.000
Whoa, look at the attitude on this one!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.660
He must be quite bold!

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.540
That's good, real good!

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.130
Oh, there goes Dad again, as usual.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.500
Are you the boss cat around here? So cute!

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.090
Hey! Which deserves your attention,
a cat or your daughter?!

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.300
Are you the boss cat around here? So cute!

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:56.480
Huh?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.450
Your dad won't come home?!

00:02:58.450 --> 00:02:59.540
Yeah...

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.940
I thought your dad's in Japan right now.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:08.410
Yeah, but as soon as he got back,
he left for Tokyo for a meeting or something.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.080
He won't stay with me at all...

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.830
Well, aren't all fathers like that?

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.290
I'm sure he has a lot to catch up on
after being away for so long.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:19.950
But you haven't seen him in two years, right?
You must miss him.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:25.050
I do... I wanted to introduce him to you all...

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:30.220
Oh! Then you should invite your
dad to the Christmas party!

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.450
Oh!

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.700
That's a great idea!

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.750
Huh...?

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:38.480
Remember? The Christmas party
that Emmy is throwing at her house!

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.610
Your dad must not have work
over the weekend, right?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.790
Right! Publishers should be closed on weekends!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.450
Good idea, thanks!

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.280
Thank you. That concludes
the process for the contract.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.500
We look forward to continuing working with you.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.170
Thank you. Well, my daughters
are waiting, so I'll...

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.920
Actually, there's an immediate project
that we would like your help with...

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.710
Project...?

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.080
Wanna stop somewhere?

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.870
Hmm.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.310
Huh? It's Takayashiki.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.160
I wonder...?

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.540
"Are you busy tomorrow? Can you go out with me?

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.900
I want to introduce you to my dad"?!

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.000
What could that mean?!

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.370
What you think it means. Congrats.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.040
Wait, wait, wait! I'm not prepared!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.370
Please! Come with me! I'm too scared!

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:41.830
I'm home!

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.040
Ah! He came home!

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:47.330
You must be hungry! I helped cook today...

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:51.800
Oh, sorry. I actually ate on the train.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.120
What?!

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.510
You have to let us know
if you're going to do that.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:59.730
Sorry about that. I'll keep that in mind!

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:03.610
What's up, Dad? You seem happy.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:07.480
Yeah, I just landed a gig that seems super fun!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.910
A gig? You mean for photography?

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.080
Yeah! You know what I'm shooting?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.660
Bears! We're following a local
hunter to take photos of bears!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.790
Anyway, I'll be in the mountains
starting tomorrow.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:25.870
What?! Tomorrow?! Tomorrow is Saturday!

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:28.250
You promised to come to
the Christmas party with us!

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.700
Oh, right... Sorry, I forgot.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.790
But this is the opportunity of a lifetime!

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:36.100
I see...

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.600
You forgot...

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.310
Aya-chan...

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.750
I'm sorry, Aya. Once I'm done with it--

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:44.790
I don't care.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:45.610
Huh?

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.320
I don't care anymore! Dad, you idiot!

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.700
What?! Hey!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:50.610
Aya-chan!

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:51.740
Aya!

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.950
That was your bad, Dad.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.120
Huh...?

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:03.790
Aya was really looking forward
to introducing her new friends to you.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.170
Oh, I see...

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:10.170
She really loves you, Dad.
That's why she's so mad.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.270
Aya-chan!

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.150
Miki-chan!

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:34.400
Um... Aya-chan...

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.080
Oh, it's raining...

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.790
So you brought her here?

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:46.950
Sorry...

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:48.500
What to do...

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.500
Excuse me...

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.010
Is my daughter here...?

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.250
Huh...? Dad?

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:55.930
Aya...!

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.700
What are you doing here?!

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:01.120
I messaged Hana-san earlier.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.750
Let's go home. Hana is waiting.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.890
No! Get away!

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.350
Aya...

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:08.790
Aya...

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:09.770
Aya-chan.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.070
If you don't want to go home,
why not play a game?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.700
I don't feel like it...

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.450
This is a game shop.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:22.450
You can stay if you're going to play,
but if not, you need to leave.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.290
A game? Now? What is he thinking?!

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.460
Fine... I'll play...

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.170
Sir, can you sit across from her?

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.040
What? Me, too?

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.930
What? Dad, too?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.910
Yeah, this is a four-player game.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:44.680
You two sit down as well,
Midori-chan, Miki-chan.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:45.830
Why don't you play then--

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.270
This is <i>Blokus.</i>

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.600
It's a territorial strategy game born in France.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:54.690
There are block pieces in
various shapes for four players.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.320
Each player takes turns
placing a piece on the board.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:01.450
The player who places the most pieces wins.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:05.870
The first piece is always placed
on your own corner of the board.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:11.500
The next piece you place needs
to touch the corner of a placed piece.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.250
You cannot touch edges.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.370
That's it.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:21.010
You can touch other players' pieces
and start with any piece.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:24.220
Let's begin.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.140
Okay, I'll start.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:31.480
<i>Blokus</i> pieces are composed
of one to five blocks.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:35.900
You lose one point for each block
on a piece you couldn't play.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:39.200
So the general strategy is
to play the bigger pieces first.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:45.410
Early on, you want to extend to the center of
the board and invade the territories of other players.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.830
I don't want to go into my dad's territory!

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:58.910
Aya! If you play pieces in your own territory
like that, you'll run out of space quickly!

00:08:58.910 --> 00:08:59.590
I don't care!

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.970
Wow, she hates me...

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:17.110
Why are you playing here?
I said I don't want you to!

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.820
Aya... Let's talk.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:25.280
There's nothing to discuss. Stay away!

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.300
I've always been a selfish man,
only doing the things I want to do.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:53.390
Whenever I find something fun,
I lose sight of everything else around me.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:10:00.530
That's right! You're selfish!
You always leave your family behind and take off!

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:02.700
That's what made Mom leave you!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.660
Aya, that's...

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:08.580
You're right. Everything is my fault.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.910
But that's who I am...

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.330
Takayashiki Kenji.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:21.340
If I change that way of life,
I would stop being me.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:26.620
If that makes you get tired of me or hate me,
there's nothing I can do.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:33.520
But no matter how much you hate me,
I will always love you.

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:37.230
I do now and I will forever.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.530
I just wanted to make sure I told you that.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.610
Dad, do you remember?

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:56.670
When I was small, I was so scared
of everything around me and cried a lot.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:02.420
But one day, you took me out to see the sunset.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.410
There, you told me,
"The world isn't a scary place.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:12.850
It's full of fun things I don't know about."

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:21.000
The world has many more fun
things you don't know about!

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.280
It's what my dad always says.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.000
From that day on, I wasn't afraid of anything.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.580
The world became a place
where I look for fun things.

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:38.170
I'll never hate you, Dad!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:43.210
I found so many fun things after that!

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:46.050
I wanted to show them to you!

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.300
Aya...

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:54.430
This shop...

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.890
These friends...

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.250
They're part of that, right?

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.350
Yes!

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.820
Come on, Dad, let's play again!

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.700
Please come again.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:12.240
Yes. Next time, I'll make sure to bring my wallet.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.580
Thanks, Manager, Miki-chan, Midori-chan!

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:17.660
Yeah.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:19.000
See you tomorrow.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.500
Yeah, see you!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:23.580
Phew.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.760
I'm glad they made up.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:27.800
But I'm surprised.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:32.010
The second game,
they both played all the pieces!

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:37.250
In <i>Blokus</i>, you have a better chance of playing more
pieces if you let the other player into your territory,

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:39.560
rather than attempt to block them.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:43.660
I guess they figured out how to let each other in.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:47.320
Manager, did you choose <i>Blokus</i>
to send that message to them?

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:52.540
What are you talking about?
Do I look like I think that way?

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:57.740
I just thought, if they're going to fight,
they should let it all out.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.880
Well then, everyone.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:15.250
Merry Christmas!

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:18.140
Let's eat, drink, and have fun tonight!

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.160
Everyone's really happy.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.200
I'm excited, too!

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.750
So, what happened to your dad?

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:28.530
Yeah, he went off after the bears!

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.790
But it's fine! I was able to
talk to him a lot last night.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.990
I won't miss him as much, even if he's gone.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:41.040
Besides, I got to introduce my best friends,
Midori-chan and Miki-chan, to him!

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:48.580
So that's what she meant by "introduce to
my dad." What did I brace myself for...

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.920
I guess I'm relieved.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:56.470
But I made a bad assumption
and dragged Ryuji into this...

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:58.640
Huh...?

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.980
Thanks for coming, Yoshioka-kun.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.870
Have fun with the games.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.190
Th-Thanks.

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:08.020
Huh... Well, good.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:13.910
Okay, let's leave the rest to Dad and enjoy!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.160
Right, then...

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.620
Yes!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.790
Actually, there's a game
I've been wanting to try!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.500
This one! <i>Ladies & Gentlemen</i>!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:30.410
Oh, the one where you compete to see
who can dress the nicest at a party in seven days!

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.220
Yes, Midori! I knew you'd know about this one.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:36.330
Sounds like fun! Let's play!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:37.550
Yes, let's!

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:41.390
Huh. Sounds like a girls' game.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:47.560
No, Shouta. This game is played as a male-female pair!

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:48.700
Male-female...

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:49.620
...pair...?

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:54.450
Yes! In this game,
the ladies must purchase the outfits.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.650
And the men?

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:00.120
The men must make money
so that the ladies can buy their dresses!

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.790
What?! That setting sounds super unfair!

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:08.580
Okay, let's split into pairs.
Since there are more girls, I'll be a gentleman.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:09.580
Pairs...?

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.800
Let's play rock-paper-scissors,
and pair up in the order that we win.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:15.880
Here we go!

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:20.180
First is rock! Rock, paper...

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.700
The result is Tanoue and Aya...

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.450
Let's win this, Tanoue-kun!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:27.850
Um, yeah...

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.750
Yoshioka-kun and Miki...

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.450
Um, good luck...

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.150
Yes, good luck.

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:35.910
And I'm paired up with Emmy.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.740
Yes! Please earn lots of money!

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.750
God!

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.450
Thank you!

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.910
In this game, the girls' and boys'
sides play at the same time.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:53.710
First, the ladies play a "Craftsman" card
in front of a shop to determine what to buy.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.510
Outfits come in four categories.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:59.620
The first one is "Dress,"
which has four types.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.910
The second is "Accessory," five types.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:06.370
The third is "Jewelry," four types.

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:09.150
The final category is "Maids,"
and there are 20 of them.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:13.370
The ladies purchase these to dress up!

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:14.610
Wow!

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:19.620
We gentlemen must make
a profit in the "Futures Market"!

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:20.280
Profit?

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:22.490
We need money to buy things.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:29.410
There are 15 tokens, which have one of six
different goods on them, facedown.

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:35.500
We all reach out at the same time to
flip them over and collect three of any type.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.750
We then sell them at the rate on the card.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:44.220
There is also a "Contract" card,
which gives a bonus to the first player to get it.

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.700
So our job is...

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:48.160
...a first come, first serve...

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.350
...action game!

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.580
I'm counting on you, Tanoue-kun!

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:53.060
Um... good luck.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.020
Y-Yeah...

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:56.980
Okay, ready?

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:58.160
Yeah.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.570
Ready... go!

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:05.830
Okay, let's go shopping!

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.540
Yay!

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:11.120
Wow, they're all so cute!

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:14.080
Yes, so many choices, it's hard to choose.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:16.830
We want them all, don't we?

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:18.050
Yes!

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:22.510
So has everyone chosen what they want?

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:26.000
Try to be cute when asking for money!

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:26.970
Okay!

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:29.330
Tanoue-kun! Buy this please!

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:31.040
That's not it, Aya!

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:31.690
Huh?

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.250
Shouta is your husband.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.650
Oh, right!

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:38.860
I really want this... Please?

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:43.250
Oh, yeah! Bring it! I'll buy you anything!

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.290
Yay!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.790
Let's see...

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:46.580
What?!

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.330
I'm way short...

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:58.000
Let's just settle for a dress today...

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.540
What?!

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:01.630
Tanoue-kun, you good-for-nothing!

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:02.800
What?!

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:08.350
Takekasa... are you sure this is all you want?

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:11.020
Um, yes... Can I buy this?

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.640
O-Of course!

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.980
She is totally being modest...

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:22.280
Thank you, Yoshioka-kun!

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.700
Midori, please!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.540
This tiara and necklace,
they're a match made in heaven!

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:34.160
No, it's too expensive. Pick one!

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:36.080
Please, darling?

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:36.880
What...?

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:40.840
You'll get some extra service
from me later... So please?

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:47.950
Fine then... Let's pay 100 libre to keep this.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:50.760
Great! I love you, darling!

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:54.350
Okay, that ends day one.

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:57.910
Five more days of shopping to go!

00:18:57.910 --> 00:18:58.810
Yeah!

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:02.110
Wait... We do this five more times?!

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:05.990
Yes, I told you the party
is in seven days, right?

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:07.910
Good luck, darling!

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.410
Um, don't work too hard...

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:12.450
Make tons of money, Tanoue-kun!

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:15.460
This isn't just a game...

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:18.540
What's being tested here is my manhood...

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.410
This match...

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:22.760
...I can't lose!

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:26.340
Here we go, day two! Ready, go!

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.660
Oh, madame.

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:58.330
What a wonderful dress you have.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.000
Where did you find it?

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.050
I have a favorite emporium.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:05.760
And you, madame, what a fabulous tiara.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:10.220
Oh, do you recognize it?
It's brand new, from Lolo Laverne.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.140
Glad to see you're all together.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:20.980
Good evening.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:22.580
Whoa...

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:23.520
So pretty...

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.580
Twenty-two, twenty-three...

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:30.030
...plus three from the maid, that's 26 points!

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:34.160
Emmy and Midori win!

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:36.910
Yay, darling! I love you!

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.000
W-Wait...

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:42.880
I'm sorry, Takekasa...
If only I made more money...

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:47.010
Don't say that! You did a lot for me...

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:52.850
Thank you, Yoshioka-kun! This is enough for me.

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:58.930
I must take good care of her
for the rest of my life...

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.650
Oh, well, we lost.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:08.070
We ended up in last place.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:11.740
Takayashiki...

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:17.750
See you later, Miki-chan!
Yoshioka-kun, take care of Miki-chan, okay?

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:18.410
Yeah.

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:20.080
Well, see you later.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.450
Okay, we should go, too.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:24.710
Y-Yeah...

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.590
I let Takayashiki down...

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:33.510
Oh, so cold! I hate the cold.

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:35.930
Oh, right...

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:40.850
Hey, take this! It's a Christmas present.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.810
A present? For me?

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:47.160
Was that too much?!

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:47.940
N-No!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:50.830
Thanks!

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:51.440
Huh?

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:57.330
I didn't expect you to get me
a present at all, so I was surprised!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.290
Right...

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:02.250
I'm so glad...

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.540
Can I open it?

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:05.000
Of course!

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:08.840
Wow, what a cute pair of gloves!

00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:10.670
So warm!

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:13.840
You've been giving me stuff all night tonight.

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:17.300
Thank you! I'm so happy.

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:22.450
So... will you forgive me now?

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:23.350
Huh?

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:27.980
I couldn't get you any gloves in the game.

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:33.030
Thank you, Yoshioka-kun,
for walking me to the station.

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:34.030
Takekasa.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.070
Huh...?

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:37.830
Um... so...

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:41.290
Say it! Say, "I want to see you again"!

00:22:43.950 --> 00:22:46.000
Um... have a happy New Year...

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:47.460
I failed...

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:53.670
Yes, see you again next year.

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:56.090
Again next year...

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:59.720
Hey, look, Yoshioka-kun!

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:06.940
Snow! It's snowing!

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:25.330
Okay, I'm leaving, too, now...

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:29.000
Darling...

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:31.130
I love you!

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:32.920
What?

00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:35.420
What?!

00:23:37.930 --> 00:23:41.680
I've decided to submit my game
to a competition in New York!

00:23:42.410 --> 00:23:44.060
I'm not running away anymore!

00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:46.350
Whatever the results may be!
